          "member": "read from the direction: \"rings\", \"ring\", \"annular\"",
          "consulted": [
            "fields[n].layout",
            "fields[n].primitive"
          ]
        },
        {
          "stage": "FOCAL_HIERARCHY",
          "why": "4 registers and sizeMax 34, both from the measured recipe rather than from a density word. Registers 1..3 carry the composition and register 0 carries the market.",
          "consulted": [
            "fields[n].sizeMax",
            "fieldCount, and the site budget"
          ]
        },
        {
          "stage": "NEGATIVE_SPACE",
          "why": "spreadMax 112 from the recipe. Spread is a CEILING the seed draws beneath from a bytecode floor of 16, which is why the recipe pins it on the later registers: unpinned, one seed in twelve draws low and is a centred island in a collection that bleeds.",
          "consulted": "fields[n].spreadMax"
        },
        {
          "stage": "RHYTHM",
          "why": "symmetry ROT6 from the recipe — it is a project constant and carries no per-token variety, which is why the recipe rather than a seed decides it; count PINNED at 18 because the drive is not COUNT",
          "consulted": [
            "fields[n].symmetry",
            "fields[n].countMin / countMax"
          ]
        },
